# The EM frames are deliberately NOT in git.
#
# They are about 1.9 GB against the 9 MB of everything else here, they never
# change once a bundle is built, and they can be regenerated from the raw EM at
# any time. So they travel once on a drive and get put in place with
# place_frames.py, while git carries only the masks and metadata, which are what
# actually change.
#
# If you find yourself about to commit a jpg, something has gone wrong.
frames/
*.jpg

# view_neurons.py's local cache (masks, meshes, and now a per-machine EM-stack
# snapshot for its "EM stack (quick)" toggle). Same reasoning as frames/ above:
# real image data, machine-specific (keyed to this machine's own WORM_PATH), and
# cheap to rebuild, so it never belongs in git.
.view_package/

# Local scratch
__pycache__/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
